<title>JORDAN: Jordan overnight rates rise to 6.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Jordan overnight rates rise to 6.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1996-11-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tighter liquidity at the start of weekly trade on Saturday pushed up overnight rates on the Jordanian dinar to 6.00 percent from 3.00-4.00 percent on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They cited heavier subscription to the Central Bank's latest CD (certificate of deposit) issue that absorbed excess funds, and higher dinar demand at the start of the month for salary transfers and bank settlements.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.7080 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Amman newsroom +962 6 623 776</p>
